 Project Overview

This project contains RESTful API implementations for 5 different questions:
- Library Book Management System
- Student Registration System
- Restaurant Menu Management
- E-Commerce Product Catalog
- Task/To-Do List Management

Each question is implemented as a separate package with its own controller and model classes.

---

 Technologies Used

- Java: 21 
- Spring Boot: 3.x
- Spring Web: REST API development
- Maven:Build tool
- Postman: API testing

---

 How to Run the Application

 Prerequisites
- Java JDK 21 or higher
- Maven (or use included Maven wrapper)
- Postman (for testing)

 Steps to Run

1. Clone the repository:
bash
   git clone <your-repository-url>
   cd restfullApiAssignment
```

2. Run the application using Maven wrapper:
   
   Windows:
bash
   mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run

   
  Mac/Linux:
```bash
   ./mvnw spring-boot:run


3. **Wait for the application to start:**
```
   Started RestfullApiAssignmentApplication in X.XXX seconds
```

4. **Application will be available at:**
```
   http://localhost:8080
```

5. **Test the APIs:**
   - Open Postman
   - Import the collection from `postman-collections/` folder
   - OR manually test endpoints listed below

---

 API Endpoints

---

 Question 1: Library Book Management API

# Base URL: `/api/books`

 1. Get All Books
- Endpoint:GET /api/books`
- Description:Retrieve all books in the library
- Response Status: 200 OK

Sample Response:*
```json
[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "title": "Clean Code",
    "author": "Robert Martin",
    "isbn": "978-0132350884",
    "publicationYear": 2008
  },
  {
    "id": 2,
    "title": "Effective Java",
    "author": "Joshua Bloch",
    "isbn": "978-0134685991",
    "publicationYear": 2018
  }
]
```

2. Get Book by ID
- Endpoint:** `GET /api/books/{id}`
- *Description:** Get a specific book by its ID
- *Path Variable:** `id` (Long)
- Response Status:** 200 OK or 404 Not Found

Sample Request:**
```
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/1
```

*Sample Response:**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Clean Code",
  "author": "Robert Martin",
  "isbn": "978-0132350884",
  "publicationYear": 2008
}
```

3. Search Books by Title
- Endpoint: `GET /api/books/search?title={title}`
- Description:Search for books by title (partial match)
- Query Parameter `title` (String)
- Response Status:** 200 OK

Sample Request:**
```
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/search?title=Clean
```

 4. Add New Book
- Endpoint:** `POST /api/books`
- Description:** Add a new book to the library
- Request Body:** Book object (JSON)
- Response Status:** 201 Created

Sample Request:**
```json
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Spring Boot in Action",
  "author": "Craig Walls",
  "isbn": "978-1617292545",
  "publicationYear": 2026
}
```

**Sample Response:**
```json
{
  "id": 4,
  "title": "Spring Boot in Action",
  "author": "Craig Walls",
  "isbn": "978-1617292545",
  "publicationYear": 2026
}
```

### 5. Delete Book
- **Endpoint:** `DELETE /api/books/{id}`
- **Description:** Delete a book by ID
- **Path Variable:** `id` (Long)
- **Response Status:** 204 No Content or 404 Not Found

**Sample Request:**
```
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/1
```

---

## Question 2: Student Registration API

### Base URL: `/api/students`

### 1. Get All Students
- **Endpoint:** `GET /api/students`
- **Response Status:** 200 OK

**Sample Response:**
```json
[
  {
    "studentId": 1,
    "firstName": "John",
    "lastName": "Doe",
    "email": "john.doe@university.edu",
    "major": "Computer Science",
    "gpa": 3.8
  }
]
```

### 2. Get Student by ID
- **Endpoint:** `GET /api/students/{studentId}`
- **Response Status:** 200 OK or 404 Not Found

### 3. Get Students by Major
- **Endpoint:** `GET /api/students/major/{major}`
- **Response Status:** 200 OK

**Sample Request:**
```
GET http://localhost:8080/api/students/major/Computer Science
```

### 4. Filter Students by GPA
- **Endpoint:** `GET /api/students/filter?gpa={minGpa}`
- **Query Parameter:** `gpa` (Double)
- **Response Status:** 200 OK

**Sample Request:**
```
GET http://localhost:8080/api/students/filter?gpa=3.5
```

### 5. Register New Student
- **Endpoint:** `POST /api/students`
- **Response Status:** 201 Created

**Sample Request:**
```json
POST http://localhost:8080/api/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "jane.smith@university.edu",
  "major": "Software Engineering",
  "gpa": 3.9
}
```

### 6. Update Student Information
- **Endpoint:** `PUT /api/students/{studentId}`
- **Response Status:** 200 OK or 404 Not Found

---

## Question 3: Restaurant Menu API

### Base URL: `/api/menu`

### Endpoints Overview

1. `GET /api/menu` - Get all menu items
2. `GET /api/menu/{id}` - Get specific menu item
3. `GET /api/menu/category/{category}` - Get items by category
4. `GET /api/menu/available?available=true` - Get available items only
5. `GET /api/menu/search?name={name}` - Search menu items by name
6. `POST /api/menu` - Add new menu item
7. `PUT /api/menu/{id}/availability` - Toggle item availability
8. `DELETE /api/menu/{id}` - Remove menu item

**Sample Menu Item Response:**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "Caesar Salad",
  "description": "Fresh romaine lettuce with parmesan cheese",
  "price": 12.99,
  "category": "Appetizer",
  "available": true
}
```

---

## Question 4: E-Commerce Product API

### Base URL: `/api/products`

### Endpoints Overview

1. `GET /api/products` - Get all products (with pagination)
2. `GET /api/products/{productId}` - Get product details
3. `GET /api/products/category/{category}` - Get products by category
4. `GET /api/products/brand/{brand}` - Get products by brand
5. `GET /api/products/search?keyword={keyword}` - Search products
6. `GET /api/products/price-range?min={min}&max={max}` - Filter by price
7. `GET /api/products/in-stock` - Get products in stock
8. `POST /api/products` - Add new product
9. `PUT /api/products/{productId}` - Update product
10. `PATCH /api/products/{productId}/stock?quantity={quantity}` - Update stock
11. `DELETE /api/products/{productId}` - Delete product

**Sample Product Response:**
```json
{
  "productId": 1,
  "name": "iPhone 15 Pro",
  "description": "Latest Apple smartphone",
  "price": 999.99,
  "category": "Electronics",
  "stockQuantity": 50,
  "brand": "Apple"
}
```

---

## Question 5: Task Management API

### Base URL: `/api/tasks`

### 1. Get All Tasks
- Endpoint:** `GET /api/tasks`
- **Response Status:** 200 OK

Sample Response:
```json
[
  {
    "taskId": 1,
    "title": "Complete Spring Boot Assignment",
    "description": "Finish all 5 questions for the REST API assignment",
    "completed": false,
    "priority": "HIGH",
    "dueDate": "2024-02-20"
  }
]
```

 2. Get Task by ID
- Endpoint: `GET /api/tasks/{taskId}`
- Response Status: 200 OK or 404 Not Found

3. Get Tasks by Status
- Endpoint:** `GET /api/tasks/status?completed={true/false}`
- Query Parameter:** `completed` (Boolean)
- Response Status:** 200 OK

Sample Request:
```
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/status?completed=true
```

 4. Get Tasks by Priority
- Endpoint: `GET /api/tasks/priority/{priority}`
- Path Variable:`priority` (String: LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH)
- Response Status:200 OK

Sample Request:
```
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/priority/HIGH
```

. Create New Task
- Endpoint: `POST /api/tasks`
- Response Status: 201 Created

Sample Request:
```json
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn Docker",
  "description": "Complete Docker tutorial",
  "completed": false,
  "priority": "MEDIUM",
  "dueDate": "2024-03-10"
}
```

 6. Update Task
- Endpoint: `PUT /api/tasks/{taskId}`
- Response Status: 200 OK or 404 Not Found

7. Mark Task as Complete
- Endpoint:PATCH /api/tasks/{taskId}/complete`
- Response Status: 200 OK or 404 Not Found

 8. Delete Task
- Endpoint: `DELETE /api/tasks/{taskId}`
- Response Status: 204 No Content or 404 Not Found

